    <!-- ── NEXT STEPS ── -->
    <section class="section" id="next-steps">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div class="section-number">12</div>
        <h2>What's Next</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">1. Google Drive integration</div>
        <p>The two Google services are scaffolded with health endpoints. The remaining work is OAuth 2.0 credential flow, token storage, and the actual Drive API calls for upload and download. Google credentials will be passed via env vars, similar to the Telegram API keys.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">2. Bulk download</div>
        <p>The UI already supports multi-select. The download service needs a <code>POST /download/bulk</code> endpoint that accepts an array of message references and queues / streams them one by one. Progress tracking via WebSocket or SSE would pair well with this.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">3. API authentication</div>
        <p>The gateway currently forwards everything without checking identity. Adding JWT middleware here means every downstream service gets auth for free — no changes needed to individual services. The gateway is the right place for cross-cutting concerns like auth, logging, and rate limiting.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">4. Download progress indicators</div>
        <p>Large video files can take time. The Angular UI should show a progress bar or at least a loading state per item. The download service could emit progress events over a WebSocket connection established at download start.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">5. Production hardening</div>
        <p>Remove debug ports from compose. Add HTTPS via a reverse proxy (Caddy or Traefik). Move secrets out of <code>.env</code> and into a secrets manager. Add proper CORS policy. Add health check conditions to <code>depends_on</code> so the gateway waits for services to be truly ready.</p>
      </div>

